// Pull request: #6667 new: DRV File Created In User AppData Folder
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6667
// Pull request author: edmundpaimon
// Change: new rule
// Title: DRV File Created In User AppData Folder
// Sigma ID: d2624ac0-1658-495b-8b90-1101fc952bf1
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Edmund
// Date: 2026-11-24 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1036
// Description: Detects the creation of a file with the ".drv" extension inside a user's AppData folder.
//   Legitimate ".drv" files are drivers and live in Windows system folders, not in user profiles.
//   Malware can use the extension to disguise a DLL. In one observed case, an Inno Setup installer
//   from a pay-per-install bundle wrote a Rust DLL named to resemble a system DLL
//   ("2iphlpapi_7.drv") to "AppData\Roaming".
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/385f0eb87b4baf68ae920bd631be18a7e812b225e183c39be6476404bc1bc081
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/27a4606f158964345275e7c714f0e5b65c108eac/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_susp_drv_file_creation_appdata.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\AppData\\" and FolderPath endswith ".drv"
